{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Text Processing \u2014 Tokenization, Stemming, Lemmatization Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: a regex word tokenizer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The simplest useful tokenizer splits on non-alphanumeric characters while keeping punctuation as its own tokens. Not perfect, not final, but it runs in one line."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import re"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tokenize(text):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z]+(?:'[A-Za-z]+)?|[0-9]+|[^\\sA-Za-z0-9]\", text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three patterns in order of precedence. Words with optional inner apostrophe (`don't`, `it's`). Pure numbers. Any single non-whitespace non-alphanumeric character as a standalone token (punctuation)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> tokenize(\"The cats weren't running at 3pm.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "['The', 'cats', \"weren't\", 'running', 'at', '3', 'pm', '.']"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Failure modes to notice. `3pm` splits to `['3', 'pm']` because we alternated between letter runs and digit runs. Good enough for most tasks. URLs, emails, hashtags all break. For production, add patterns before the general ones."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: a Porter stemmer (step 1a only)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The full Porter algorithm has five phases of rules. Step 1a alone covers the most frequent English suffixes and teaches the pattern."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def stem_step_1a(word):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if word.endswith(\"sses\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return word[:-2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if word.endswith(\"ies\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return word[:-2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if word.endswith(\"ss\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return word"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if word.endswith(\"s\") and len(word) > 1:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return word[:-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return word"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> [stem_step_1a(w) for w in [\"caresses\", \"ponies\", \"caress\", \"cats\"]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "['caress', 'poni', 'caress', 'cat']"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Read the rules top-down. The `ies -> i` rule is why `ponies -> poni`, not `pony`. Real Porter has step 1b that would fix it. Rules compete. Earlier rules win. The order matters more than any single rule."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: a lookup-based lemmatizer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Lemmatization proper needs morphology. A tractable teaching version uses a small lemma table and a fallback."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "LEMMA_TABLE = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"running\", \"VERB\"): \"run\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"ran\", \"VERB\"): \"run\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"runs\", \"VERB\"): \"run\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"better\", \"ADJ\"): \"good\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"best\", \"ADJ\"): \"good\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"cats\", \"NOUN\"): \"cat\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"cat\", \"NOUN\"): \"cat\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"were\", \"VERB\"): \"be\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"was\", \"VERB\"): \"be\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"is\", \"VERB\"): \"be\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def lemmatize(word, pos):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    key = (word.lower(), pos)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if key in LEMMA_TABLE:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return LEMMA_TABLE[key]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if pos == \"VERB\" and word.endswith(\"ing\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return word[:-3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if pos == \"NOUN\" and word.endswith(\"s\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return word[:-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return word.lower()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> lemmatize(\"running\", \"VERB\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "'run'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> lemmatize(\"cats\", \"NOUN\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "'cat'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> lemmatize(\"better\", \"ADJ\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "'good'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> lemmatize(\"watched\", \"VERB\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "'watched'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The last case is the key teaching moment. `watched` is not in our table and our fallback only handles `ing`. Real lemmatization covers `ed`, irregular verbs, comparative adjectives, plurals with sound changes (`children -> child`). This is why production systems use WordNet, spaCy's morphologizer, or a full morphological analyzer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: pipe them together"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def preprocess(text, pos_tagger=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens = tokenize(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    stems = [stem_step_1a(t.lower()) for t in tokens]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tags = pos_tagger(tokens) if pos_tagger else [(t, \"NOUN\") for t in tokens]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    lemmas = [lemmatize(word, pos) for word, pos in tags]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return {\"tokens\": tokens, \"stems\": stems, \"lemmas\": lemmas}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The missing piece is a POS tagger. Phase 5 \u00b7 07 (POS Tagging) builds one. For now, default everything to `NOUN` and acknowledge the limitation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Extend `tokenize` to keep URLs as single tokens. Test: `tokenize(\"Visit https://example.com today.\")` should produce one URL token.\n2. **Medium.** Implement Porter step 1b. If a word contains a vowel and ends in `ed` or `ing`, remove it. Handle the double-consonant rule (`hopping -> hop`, not `hopp`).\n3. **Hard.** Build a lemmatizer that uses WordNet as a lookup table but falls back to your Porter stemmer when WordNet has no entry. Measure accuracy on a tagged corpus against plain WordNet and plain Porter."
      ]
    }
